    "notes": [
      "The idea is only half delivered. 'Bamburgh' does fill columns 1–12 across rows 2–4, but the photo also spans the full 12 columns, so the castle reads as wide as the name. The contrast between a small village and a vast castle is lost. Crop the photo tighter around the castle and crag so the castle fills more of its frame, and keep the village houses small at the bottom edge.",
      "Row 4 is mostly empty. The headline's descender 'g' dips into it, but the space between the baseline of 'Bamburgh' and the top of the photo at row 5 is close to a full module and looks accidental. Either pull the photo up to start in row 4 so the castle sits directly beneath the name, as the idea says, or let the headline grow to fill rows 2–4.",
      "The photo spans rows 5–9 (5 rows) at full width, so it becomes a flat landscape band. The castle occupies only about columns 4–9 inside it, and the upper sky takes nearly half the frame. Crop out most of the sky so the crag rises toward row 5. One option: set the photo to columns 1–12 in rows 4–9 with the castle top just under the headline.",
      "The lead starts at column 4 and runs through column 12, a 9-column measure. At this size that gives roughly 50 characters per line, which is fine. Its first baseline aligns with the county label in row 10. Keep both.",
      "The body text in columns 4–8, row 12, is cut off from the lead by an empty row 11. This reads as a hole, not a deliberate empty module. Move the body up to row 11 directly under the lead, so the empty space falls into row 12 above the footer. Or keep it in row 12 and widen it to columns 4–9 so it aligns with the footer's 'Country' column.",
      "The pinfield in columns 1–3, rows 11–12, is too small and faint to read as a map. The highlighted Bamburgh pin sits in the top-left corner of the module and the scatter drifts toward the footer. Either enlarge it to fill both rows fully, with the highlight pin aligned to the lead's first line, or drop it so columns 1–3 of rows 11–12 become a clean empty module.",
      "The vertical rhythm is uneven. The gaps between header, headline, photo and text are all different. Lock each element's top to a row line: headline cap height on the row 2 top, photo top on a row start, lead cap height on the row 10 top.",
      "On color, the blue of the county label and the pin picks up the sky and sea, which is good. But the saturated green field across the lower third of the photo is the loudest area on the page and pulls the eye down. Crop the foreground field so the lower edge of the photo sits closer to the village. The warm stone of the castle then becomes the colour focus under the black headline."
    ],
    "summary": "This is a clean, competent layout with a strong full-width headline and a sensible text block. But the stated contrast between a small village and a vast castle doesn't come through. The full-width landscape photo has too much sky and field, so it flattens the castle. Fix the gap in rows 4 and 11 and crop the photo vertically toward the crag, and this becomes a keeper.",
    "mean": 6.4
  },
